  "slug": "degeneration-il-68cc",
  "summary": "Single-cell and snRNA-seq studies now resolve senescent endothelial and fibro-inflammatory adipose subpopulations underlying vascular and metabolic disease.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is cell-type-resolved profiling of vascular and adipose tissue, where single-cell transcriptomics isolates disease- or age-associated subpopulations rather than bulk averages. In aged murine perigonadal adipose, snRNA-seq identifies senescent capillary endothelial nuclei marked by Mif overexpression, with ion channel expression linked to an endothelial senotype. In human visceral adipose across lean, obese, and obese-T2D states, a THBS1-high fibro-inflammatory stromal and adipocyte subpopulation is identified as a potential driver of fibro-inflammation in metabolic disease. Reanalysis of diabetic gingiva scRNA-seq resolves four fibroblast states, with expanded inflammatory fibroblasts and state-specific purinergic remodeling. Lipidomics of atherosclerosis and abdominal aortic aneurysm shows distinct lipid class enrichment, with Acadm-mediated fatty acid β-oxidation implicated.",
